\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar interbank rates could meet or overshoot U.S. rates, says \uc2 HKMA\b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2023\par 12:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, June 14 (Reuters) - Hong Kong dollar interbank rates could catch up with, or even overshoot their U.S. dollar counterparts as companies' demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for dividend payments peaks in the three months to August, the head of the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 This is a seasonal factor unique to Hong Kong that affects the city's interbank rates, as listed companies need to stock up on Hong Kong dollars to pay dividends, said \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Chief Executive \uc2 Eddie Yue\uc2  in an "Insight" article published on its website on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The peak season for dividend payments is usually in June to August. Such funding demand sends the Hong Kong dollar exchange rate higher, he said.\par \par \uc2 Such seasonal factors will continue to influence interbank rates in the coming weeks or months, Yue said.\par \par \uc2 "The possibility that HKD interbank rates will catch up with, or even overshoot, their USD counterparts on certain days cannot be ruled out," said Yue.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar was up 30 pips on Wednesday, at 7.8308 per dollar and the highest in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong overnight interbank offered rate reversed two straight days of decline and rose to 3.88%, the highest since May 30, after having peaked at nearly 5% on May 19 at a nearly 16-year high.\par \par \uc2 Seasonal factors aside, Hong Kong's interbank rate is affected by the U.S. interest rate trend due to the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the greenback. The Hong Kong dollar is pegged within a band of 7.75 to 7.85 versus the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 A widening of the interest rate gap between the Hong Kong dollar and U.S. dollar had incentivized carry trades and weakened the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, thereby leading to over 40 rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  since the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  began hiking rates in March 2022 up to May.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Georgina Lee; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-14T11:50:10.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230614ej6e01i0p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
