\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Hong Kong interbank rates jump ahead of Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2023\par 12:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3-month HIBOR jumps 18.9 bps, sharpest leap since May 2020\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Traders anticipate further liquidity drain\par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 HKMA\uc2  statement)\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 3 (Reuters) - Hong Kong interbank rates jumped sharply on Wednesday as months of authorities sucking cash from the financial system took effect, and as traders braced for a U.S. interest rate hike.\par \par \uc2 The three-month Hong Kong Interbank Offered Rate (HIBOR) jumped 18.9 basis points (bps) to 3.89929%, its sharpest one-day leap in nearly two years. One-month HIBOR rose more than 14 bps to 3.55333%, its highest since January.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong and U.S. rates markets are tethered by the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Since February the Hong Kong dollar has been at the weak end of its tight trading band, obliging the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 HKMA\uc2 ) to buy Hong Kong dollars, which makes them scarcer and eventually applies upward pressure on interbank rates.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's aggregate balance -- a gauge of cash levels in the banking system -- has declined precipitously as the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the peg, hitting a 14-1/2 year low of HK$49 billion ($6.2 billion).\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong rates have been creeping up for about two weeks, as the reduction of cash in the financial system starts flowing through to banks. Analysts said Wednesday's sudden move was in anticipation of a U.S. hike driving another round of HKMA Hong Kong dollar buying.\par \par \uc2 "The market is overall getting slightly more cautious about interbank cash balance falling further," said Ju Wang, head of Greater China \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rates strategy at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jumps in HIBOR also reflect market participants positioning for Hong Kong rates to close a wide gap on U.S. rates, she said.\par \par \uc2 The difference, or spread, between HIBOR rates and U.S. dollar equivalents hit its widest in almost two decades in April as sluggish loan demand offset the \uc2 HKMA\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and kept \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  flush with cash.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  is\par \par \uc2 expected\par \par \uc2 to raise the benchmark Fed funds rate by 25 bps on Wednesday and perhaps hint that its hiking cycle is all but over.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar was pinned at the weak end of its band at 7.8499 to the greenback on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HKMA\uc2  issued a\par \par \uc2 statement\par \par \uc2 late in the afternoon, saying it "continues to have strong confidence in the linked exchange rate system", and adding banks have been able to properly manage their liquidity and ensure the orderly movements of funds.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 7.8499 Hong Kong dollars) (Reporting by Georgina Lee in Hong Kong. Writing by Tom Westbrook; Editing by Andrew Heavens and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-3T11:47:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230503ej5301nst\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
