\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 HKMA\uc2  buys more than $905 mln to shore up local  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  at bottom of trading band\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2023\par 03:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Add analysts comment, interbank interest rate levels)\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, April 4 (Reuters) - Hong Kong's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought HK$7.104 billion ($905 million) worth of U.S. dollars during New York's Monday trading hours to stop the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening beyond its target range.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged within a band of 7.75 to 7.85 versus the U.S. dollar. It touched 7.85 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The aggregate balance - the main gauge of cash in Hong Kong's banking system - will fall to HK$69.915 billion on April 6, an \uc2 HKMA\uc2  spokesperson said on Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 HKMA\uc2 ) has bought the equivalent of $34.2 billion since 2022 in 44 rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  began hiking interest rates last March.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong banking system remains flush with cash due to a lack of popular initial public offerings (IPOs), which used to lock up large amount of subscription money from retail investors and squeeze short-term interbank borrowing costs, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Combined with weak loan demand, banks' appetite for funding remains low. Hong Kong interbank rates therefore continue to hover at a discount compared to U.S. interbank rates despite the multiple rounds of \uc2 HKMA\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  squeezing the banking system's cash balances, said Ken Cheung, chief Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Mizhuho Bank.\par \par \uc2 "Before the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  pauses its current interest rate cycle I'd expect the Hong Kong dollar to remain volatile, and hover in the weaker-half of a trading band at 7.8 to 7.85," said Cheung.\par \par \uc2 One-month Hibor was at 3.09530% on Monday, down from the peak of 5.08208% in December. That represents a discount of about 176 basis points (bps) below equivalent tenor U.S. Libor, down from the 247 bps seen in mid-February which was widest discount in more than 15 years.\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's Linked Exchange Rate System, the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  is committed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain the peg whenever the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar weakens or strengthens to either end of the trading band.\par \par \uc2 "We expect Hong Kong dollar rates to bottom out on thinner aggregate balance following the \uc2 HKMA\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and upcoming IPOs," latter this year, said \uc2 Mizuho\uc2 's Cheung.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 7.8478 Hong Kong dollars) (Reporting by Donny Kwok and Georgina Lee; Editing by Christopher Cushing and Tom Hogue) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-4-4T02:39:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230404ej44001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
