\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 HKMA\uc2  buys HK$4.22 bln from market as  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  hits low end of trading band\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2023\par 03:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Add banker's comment and interbank rate levels)\par \par \uc2 By Donny Kwok and Georgina Lee\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Hong Kong's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday that it had bought HK$4.223 billion ($538 million) from the market during New York trading hours on Monday to stop the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening and breaking its peg to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to a tight band of between 7.75 and 7.85 versus the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The aggregate balance - the key gauge of cash balances in the banking system - will decrease to HK$91.864 billion on Feb. 15, a \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 HKMA\uc2 ) spokesperson said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The latest move to defend the peg came after \uc2 HKMA\uc2  bought the equivalent of $30.9 billion of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the market in 2022 through 41 rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  began hiking interest rates last March.\par \par \uc2 Such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at one point firmed up \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank offer rates (Hibor), including the one-month and three-month tenors, and even exceeded U.S. interbank offer rates of the same tenors in early December. But the rates dropped heading into 2023.\par \par \uc2 Three-month Hibor fell to 3.42958% on Monday from a peak of 5.4% in December, representing a discount of about 140 basis point below equivalent tenor U.S. Libor, the widest discount in 16 years.\par \par \uc2 This has revived interest from some investors in borrowing Hong Kong dollars to fund their purchases of higher-yielding U.S. dollar assets, and weighed on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to bankers.\par \par \uc2 "The still-recovering Hong Kong economy and low demand from corporates and individuals for loans has continued to weigh on Hibor. The Hong Kong dollar banking system is flushed with liquidity," said Patrick Wu, co-head of trading for Asia Pacific and the Middle East at Credit Agricole-CIB.\par \par \uc2 In the fourth quarter of 2022, Hong Kong's economy contracted 4.2% from a year earlier, the second-deepest decline since the second quarter of 2020 when COVID-19 took a toll around the world.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 7.8499 Hong Kong dollars) (Reporting by Donny Kwok and Georgina Lee; Editing by Leslie Adler and Jamie Freed) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-14T03:02:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230214ej2e00bq9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
