\par\par \b \uc2 EXPLAINER-What's behind Hong Kong's tightening cash conditions?\b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2022\par 08:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 3 (Reuters) - A weak Hong Kong dollar and capital outflows have pushed the city's interbank rates to 14-year highs and drained cash levels to their lowest in two years, sparking investor worries about Hong Kong's cherished \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg and its economic health.\par \par \uc2 Below are some details on the complex policy framework and recent developments surrounding the tight liquidity: WHY IS HONG KONG ON INVESTORS' RADAR?\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's aggregate balance, a gauge of cash levels in the banking system, has been declining rapidly since May and is about to drop below HK$100 billion ($12.74 billion) for the first time in two years.\par \par \uc2 The decline in the aggregate balance has come alongside a drop in the Hong Kong dollar to the weak end of its trading band, driven by aggressive U.S. monetary tightening, capital outflows and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the defacto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 HKMA\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 That has tightened cash in the economy and driven the one-month Hong Kong Interbank Offer Rate (HIBOR) to a 14-year high. WHY ARE CASH CONDITIONS SO TIGHT?\par \par \uc2 A dearth of initial public offerings this year on \uc2 Hong Kong Exchanges & Clearing\uc2 's (\uc2 HKEX\uc2 ) markets has dampened investor demand for Hong Kong dollars. Total IPO funds raised on the exchange plunged 74% year-on-year to HK$73.2 billion ($9.33 billion) for the first nine months this year, \uc2 HKEX\uc2  data shows.\par \par \uc2 There has also been an outflow of foreign investment from Hong Kong equities, funds and bonds. Their combined balance in Hong Kong's international investment position, which is the external balance sheet, dropped by 3% to HK$3.99 trillion as of June compared with the end of 2021, official data shows.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong dollar interbank liquidity has tightened accordingly. The aggregate balance, a key measure of the interbank cash balance, has also been depleted by 40 rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  this year. HOW ARE \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2  INTEREST RATES DETERMINED?\par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's Linked Exchange Rate System, the Hong Kong dollar is pegged in a tight band between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar, and the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  is committed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain the band.\par \par \uc2 As outflows from \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  picked up, the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  has been forced to buy the local dollar and sell U.S. dollars to prevent it from weakening past 7.85.\par \par \uc2 HKMA\uc2 's buying of Hong Kong dollars shrank the aggregate balance from HK$233.49 billion in June to HK$100.03 bln on Thursday, resulting in higher Hibor rates.\par \par \uc2 The overnight Hibor, which reflects financial institutions' demand for cash, spiked to 3.028% on Oct 31, the highest in nearly three years. Hibor is influenced mainly by capital flows in and out of Hong Kong, as the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  does not set interest rates. IS THE FALL IN BANKING SYSTEM LIQUIDITY A CAUSE FOR CONCERN?\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are down $33 bln since May, they remain ample at $419.2 billion. Also, with fiscal buffers in the form of exchange bills, the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  can fend off any notion of pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, Hong Kong's monetary Base, at HK$1.9 trillion, is fully backed by U.S. dollar assets.\par \par \uc2 But home owners with mortgages will face larger interest payments as Hibor, which is the benchmark that banks use, rises. The \uc2 HKMA\uc2  said cases of negative equity in Hong Kong's residential mortgage loans registered a near ninefold increase in the third quarter from the prior quarter. HOW FAR WILL \uc2 HKMA\uc2  LET THE AGGREGATE BALANCE FALL?\par \par \uc2 The last time the aggregate balance fell below HK$100 billion was in June 2020, and before that during the last U.S. rate-hike cycle from 2017 to 2019, when the aggregate balance hit HK$54 billion.\par \par \uc2 The impact on the HK dollar peg had been muted, the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Even if the aggregate balance were to drop to zero, the Linked Exchange Rate System will not be affected as \uc2 HKMA\uc2  can mobilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to support the peg. ($1 = 7.8498 Hong Kong dollars)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Georgina Lee; Editing by Vidya Ranganathan and Edmund Klamann) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-11-3T08:25:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221103eib300qs4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
