y, such as, credit risk scores, collateral and collection history. Individual credit scores are assessed by credit bureau, such as TransUnion. Internal risk grade ratings reflect the credit quality of the borrower, as well as the value of collateral held as security. The Company requires collateral arrangements to all mortgage loans and has policies and procedures for validating the reasonableness of the collateral valuations on a regular basis. Management believes that these policies effectively manage the credit risk from advances.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 COSMOS GROUP HOLDINGS INC.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTES TO UNAUDITED CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FOR THE THREE AND NINE MONTHS ENDED SEPTEMBER 30, 2022 AND 2021\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expressed in United States Dollars ("US$"), except for number of shares)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company's internally assigned risk grades are as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pass: Loans are of acceptable risk.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Assets Especially Mentioned (OAEM): Loans have potential weaknesses that deserve management's close attention.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Substandard: Loans reflect significant deficiencies due to several adverse trends of a financial, economic or managerial nature.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Doubtful: Loans have all the weaknesses inherent in a substandard loan with added characteristics that make collection or liquidation in full based on currently existing facts, conditions and values highly questionable or improbable.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Loss: Loans have been identified for charge-off because they are considered uncollectible and of such little value that their continuance as bankable assets is not warranted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table presents credit quality exposures by internally assigned risk ratings as of the dates indicated:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit grades       