\par\par \b \uc2 EXCLUSIVE-China's state banks told to stock up for yuan  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -sources\b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2022\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 29 (Reuters) - \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has asked major state-owned banks to be prepared to sell dollars for the local unit in offshore markets as it steps up efforts to stem the yuan's descent, four sources with knowledge of the matter said.\par \par \uc2 State banks were told to ask their offshore branches, including those based in Hong Kong, New York and London, to review their holdings of the offshore yuan and ensure U.S. dollar reserves are ready to be deployed, three of the sources, who declined to be identified, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The simultaneous selling of dollars and buying of yuan could put a floor under the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has lost more than 11% to the dollar so far this year and looks set for its biggest annual loss since 1994, when China unified its official and market rates.\par \par \uc2 The scale of this round of dollar selling to defend the weakening yuan will be rather big, one of the sources said.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  did not immediately respond to a Reuters request for comment. (Reporting by Julie Zhu in Hong Kong, and Shanghai & Beijing newsrooms; Editing by Vidya Ranganathan and Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-2T09:27:50.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220929ei9t01rw1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
