\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Hong Kong interbank rate touches 2-year high as \uc2 HKMA\uc2  withdraws cash\b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2022\par 07:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, comments; paragraphs 5-11)\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, July 22 (Reuters) - Hong Kong dollar rates jumped on Friday, as heavy buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the global financial hub drained liquidity and investors braced for the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  to raise rates sharply next week.\par \par \uc2 Rates in Hong Kong tend to move in lockstep with U.S. rates, as its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pegged to the greenback, although they have lagged their U.S. equivalents in recent months.\par \par \uc2 The one-month Hong Kong interbank offered rate, or Hibor - a benchmark for pricing mortgages in one of the world's most expensive property markets - advanced for a seventh straight trading session on Friday to 1.01143%, its highest since May 2020.\par \par \uc2 Other tenors ranging from three-month to one-year Hibor also gained.\par \par \uc2 Rising funding costs came as the Hong Kong dollar kept hitting the weaker side of its trading band, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and withdraw the unit.\par \par \uc2 As a result, \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggregate balance, a gauge of liquidity in its banking system, has fallen to a two-year low of HK $165.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 "Hibor is playing some catch-up with the previous increases in USD Libor, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interbank liquidity is shrinking upon \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ahead of the FOMC next week," said Frances Cheung, a rates strategist at \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "Higher HKD rates are part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -interest rate adjustment process, but, as the still supportive interbank liquidity is preventing HKD rates from rising more aggressively, this \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -interest rate adjustment is not done yet."\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to a tight band between 7.75 and 7.85 against the U.S. dollar, and the Fed's monetary tightening, more hawkish than previously anticipated, has driven up U.S. yields and piled depreciation pressure on it.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought HK$ 173 billion of its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the market this year, its data shows.\par \par \uc2 The current linked exchange rate system obliges the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  to buy its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid breaching the weaker limit of 7.85. (Reporting by Winni Zhou, Tom Westbrook and Alun John; Editing by Jacqueline Wong and Clarence Fernandez) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-22T06:38:40.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220722ei7m00mdl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
