\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong \highlight\uc2  c.bank props up  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 , first  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  since Oct 2020\b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2022\par 13:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details of second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Donny Kwok and Alun John\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 12 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 HKMA\uc2 ) stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in 18 months, twice buying Hong Kong dollars to stop the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening and breaking its peg to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought HK$1.586 billion ($202 million) from the market in U.S trading on Wednesday and a further HK$4.082 billion in Hong Kong trading on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to a tight band of between 7.75 and 7.85 versus the U.S. dollar. It has been softening as U.S. interest rates rise while a surfeit of cash in the local banking system keeps Hong Kong rates pinned down.\par \par \uc2 One-month U.S. dollar Libor, a benchmark lending rate, is around 0.8% - its highest since April 2020 - while the Hong Kong equivalent, one-month Hibor, is under 0.2% and barely above its COVID-19 pandemic lows.\par \par \uc2 HKMA\uc2 's Chief Executive \uc2 Eddie Yue\uc2  said last week that as it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  and funds flow out of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's system, local rates should rise, removing the incentive for market players to conduct "carry trades", and hence keep the Hong Kong dollar trading within its band.\par \par \uc2 "All these are normal \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in accordance with the design of the Linked Exchange Rate System," he said.\par \par \uc2 This arrangement was created in 1983 and has survived many crises over the years, including an attack from famed short-seller George Soros during the 1997-98 Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HKMA\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October 2020. That year it sold HK$383.5 billion worth to rein in the strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to \uc2 HKMA\uc2  data, while it last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the weak end of the band in March 2019.\par \par \uc2 After both \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the aggregate balance - the key gauge of cash in the banking system - will decrease to HK$331.923 billion on May 16, an \uc2 HKMA\uc2  spokeswoman said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 It dropped to around HK$50 billion in 2019 after the last series of \uc2 HKMA\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, it surged to more than HK$450 billion as capital rushed into Hong Kong, drawn by higher interest rates locally than in the U.S. and a series of large initial public offerings. (Reporting by Donny Kwok; Editing by Stephen Coates, Kenneth Maxwell and Bernadette Baum) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-5-12T12:17:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220511ei5b04wme\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
