\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firms on safety flows, euro looks past Macron's victory\b0\par\par\uc2 710 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2022\par 06:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, April 25 (Reuters) - The dollar climbed on Monday as investors sought safety due to uncertainties over the global growth outlook, gaining ground even on the euro despite French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 's comfortable election victory over far-right rival \uc2 Marine Le Pen\uc2 Marine Le Pen.               \par \par \uc2 The dollar index rose 0.2% to 101.3 testing last week's two-year peak of 101.33.               \par \par \uc2 "With the French election out of the way the market is starting to focus on other worries. Stock markets are in the red this morning, and that risk aversion has generally benefitted the dollar, and this why the euro has been dragged a bit lower," said Sim Moh Siong, \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist, at \uc2 Bank of Singapore\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "There are three big forces driving the markets and all are worries," he said, pointing to fears about whether the U.S. and global economy can withstand an increasingly hawkish \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , worries about Chinese growth due to lockdowns to prevent the spread of COVID-19 and the commodity shock caused by the Russia-Ukraine war.               \par \par \uc2 The euro fell 0.29% to $1.0778, after initially opening higher, and is not far from the two-year low of $1.0758 hit last week.               \par \par \uc2 However it gained 0.12% against sterling, touching a one-month peak of 84.32 pence in early trade.               \par \par \uc2 With 97% of votes counted, Macron was on course for a solid 57.4% of the vote, interior ministry figures showed. In his victory speech he acknowledged that many people had only voted for him only to keep \uc2 Le Pen\uc2  out, and he promised to address the sense of many French that their living standards were slipping.               \par \par \uc2 Markets had worried that a Le Pen victory, which was not predicted by the polls, would lead to significant economic change in the euro zone's second-largest economy.               \par \par \uc2 "Macron's clear victory is likely to reassure the markets that the European dynamic will continue," said Frederic Leroux, a member of the investment team at Carmignac.               \par \par \uc2 Sterling fell 0.3% against the dollar to $1.28085, a fresh low since September 2020.               \par \par \uc2 The pound has been hurt by last week's weak British retail sales and consumer-confidence data and \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  comments that signalled a possible slowdown in the expected upward movement of interest rates.                              \par \par \uc2 CHINA FEARS               \par \par \uc2 China's yuan fell to a one-year low on Monday extending losses after posting its worst week since 2015, as investors fret about the worsening economic growth outlook due to strict COVID-19 measures and lockdowns across the country.               \par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 set the midpoint rate on Monday at 6.4909 per dollar prior to market open, the weakest since August 2021. In the spot market, both the onshore and offshore yuan, touched their weakest since April 2021.               \par \par \uc2 On Monday, Beijing began three rounds of COVID-19 testing for all residents of its biggest district Chaoyang after dozens of cases were reported, prompting people to stock up on food over fears of an eventual strict lockdown akin to that in the financial hub of Shanghai.               \par \par \uc2 "The (Chinese) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to weaken last week on the back of lockdowns and the restrained approach to interest rate cuts," said \uc2 Bank of Singapore\uc2 's Sim, adding it was not surprising this had affected the Australian dollar. Australia's resource-rich economy is especially tied to Chinese demand.               \par \par \uc2 The Aussie fell 1% to $0.7165, its lowest in a month.               \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar, which is pegged in a tight band against the U.S. dollar dropped to as low as HK$7.8475 per dollar. It is almost at the HK$7.85 level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 Among major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Japanese yen has been the most affected by rising U.S. interest rates, with Japan keeping its benchmark yields pinned down at ultra-low rates. On Monday morning, the dollar was weaker against the yen at 128.33.               \par \par \uc2 The dollar has gained 11% on the yen so far this year. Last week's 129.4 was the highest for dollar-yen in 20 years.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-4-25T05:57:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220425ei4p00o6t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
