\par\par \b \uc2 BREAKINGVIEWS-Giant Ant frustrates Hong Kong dollar bears\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2020\par 03:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (The author is a Reuters Breakingviews columnist. The opinions expressed are her own. Refiles to add stock codes.)\par \par \uc2 By Jennifer Hughes\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Sept 24 (Reuters Breakingviews) - Pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are irresistible to speculators, and the Hong Kong dollar\u8217\'20\'19s 36-year-old fix is no different. Since political strife erupted in the territory last year, investors like Kyle Bass, founder of Dallas-based Hayman Capital Management, have been betting that capital flight will break a narrow band. But Ant Group\u8217\'20\'19s $30 billion-plus float and other expected Chinese technology listings are drawing inflows, strengthening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and creating headaches for doomsayers.\par \par \uc2 Demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars has triggered near-daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Sept. 14. Brokers say interest in securing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of Ant\u8217\'20\'19s expected October float has been a key driver. The city is used to seeing liquidity tighten ahead of big deals and this one boasts size and brings expectations that more will follow. Inflows could easily top $100 billion for the Hong Kong leg of the dual listing, which could see $17.5 billion of shares on offer in the city, according to sources cited by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Speculators reckon Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s standing as a financial centre will be damaged by Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s hardening grip on the territory and by rising U.S.-China tensions. Officials in Washington in June even discussed undermining the peg, according to Bloomberg reports. Bears are also wary that any sharp sustained outflows from the city\u8217\'20\'19s banking system, given its large size relative to the local economy, could easily overwhelm the HKMA\u8217\'20\'19s defences.\par \par \uc2 But as U.S. sentiment has soured on the People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic, inflows to Hong Kong have followed. A series of New York-listed Chinese companies have sold additional shares in the city, creating a funding alternative should Washington push ahead with threats to delist them. Secondary listings from Netease and \uc2 JD.com\uc2  in June attracted bids worth 10 times the combined $6.6 billion they raised. Ant\u8217\'20\'19s IPO will only add to the city\u8217\'20\'19s fresh pull.\par \par \uc2 The result is what ANZ analysts call a \u8220\'20\'1Cheadquarters effect\u8221\'20\'1D where stock-specific inflows into smaller economies warp traditional measures of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength such as current account balances and reserves. South Korea and Taiwan, home to \uc2 Samsung\uc2  and TSMC, are two such examples. Hong Kong has the makings of another. Either way, the current run of Ant-related inflows may well last long enough to frustrate the bears.\par \par \uc2 On Twitter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JennHughes13"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/JennHughes13}}}\par \par \uc2 CONTEXT NEWS\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost daily since Sept. 14 to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breaking the strong side of its HK$7.75-to-HK$7.85 range peg to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 - China\u8217\'20\'19s Ant Group plans to raise $35 billion in an initial public offering, Reuters reported on Sept. 23, citing sources. The company will raise half the amount in Hong Kong, and the other half on Shanghai\u8217\'20\'19s STAR market.\par \par \uc2 - For previous columns by the author, Reuters customers can click on\par \par \uc2 - SIGN UP FOR BREAKINGVIEWS EMAIL ALERTS: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://bit.ly/BVsubscribe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://bit.ly/BVsubscribe}}}\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Una Galani and Katrina Hamlin) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-9-24T02:52:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200924eg9o00795\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
