\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2020\par 06:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Dollar's Surge Spurs HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peg to the U.S. dollar, selling the Hong Kong dollar after it hit the strong end of the trading band against the greenback. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2   Sees 5.2% Decline in Global Economy in 2020 From Coronavirus \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The global economy is expected to shrink by about 5.2% in 2020 as a result of the coronavirus pandemic, making it one of the four most severe downturns in 150 years, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Behind \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Rare Foray Into Politics Over Hong Kong \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a century and a half trying to steer a neutral course through the messy geopolitics of east versus west, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has signaled its support for China over the future of Hong Kong. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par In the Feud Between Two of U.K.'s Richest Men, Family Members Say They Bugged Uncle \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Several members of Britain's billionaire Barclay family admitted to bugging their uncle and cousin, in a court case related to the sale of London's Ritz Hotel that has split the secretive clan. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Relief Spreads to Risky European Bank Bonds \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European bank bonds have rallied over the past few weeks, escaping crisis territory thanks to the easing of coronavirus lockdowns and the proposed launch of a \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  -wide recovery fund. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Nasdaq  Overtakes NYSE in Coronavirus-Era IPOs \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq has edged past the NYSE in IPOs this year as the coronavirus pandemic has curtailed activity and reined in celebrations of corporate debuts on the NYSE's historic trading floor. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Wall Street Has No Consensus \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Forecasts from analysts about the market and economy are ranging from financial Armageddon to a swift second-half recovery. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Financial Services Roundup: Market Talk \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest Market Talks covering Financial Services \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed Debates Whether to Reinforce Low-Rate Pledge With Yield Caps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve officials are studying Australia's program to buy government securities in unlimited quantities to peg some yields at low levels. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par People Aren't Visiting Branches. Banks Are Wondering How Many They Still Need. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pandemic has forced people used to visiting branches to bank on apps and online instead. That shift could speed up plans for closing many branches permanently.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 09, 2020 00:00 ET (04:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020200609eg690004s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
