\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong Dollar Hits Trading Band Ceiling\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joanne Chiu \par \uc2 525 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2020\par 14:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rallied to its strongest levels last seen since 2015, even as the coronavirus pandemic hit the economic outlook in the semiautonomous city.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the strong side of its trading band. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg permits the Hong Kong dollar to trade between HK$7.75 and HK$7.85 to the U.S. dollar, and that the city's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertakes to buy or sell the local unit whenever it touches either side of the band.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has injected liquidity into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling 1.55 billion Hong Kong dollars ($200 million) to investors, as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits the upper limit of where it is allowed to trade against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The authority last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the weakest side of the trading band during 2018 and 2019, as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tested the level of 7.85 a dollar. When the Hong Kong dollar falls to the weakest side of the trading band it would sell U.S. dollars for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to drain Hong Kong dollars from the market.\par \par \uc2 Gary Ng, an economist at \uc2 Natixis\uc2  in Hong Kong, said tight liquidity conditions and interest rate differential are what drove the Hong Kong dollar stronger.\par \par \uc2 A widening gap between local borrowing costs and those in the U.S. offer "a lucrative carry trade opportunity" to investors, he said.\par \par \uc2 The rally of the Hong Kong dollar came despite credit rating agency \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  on April 20 downgraded the city's credit rating to AA- from AA with a stable outlook. It said the city faces a "second major shock" from the coronavirus after prolonged social unrest last year.\par \par \uc2 Fitch forecasts Hong Kong's GDP in real terms will fall by 5% in 2020, following a 1.2% decline in 2019.\par \par \uc2 Ken Cheung, chief Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Bank\uc2 , said despite a weaker economic outlook, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "is still seen by many investors as a safer bet" because of its peg with the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The credit-rating downgrade by Fitch and deteriorating economic data have clouded the outlook of Hong Kong-dollar assets but it is unlikely to undermine the stability of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg with the greenback in the near term, as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is fully backed up by funds including the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Eddie Yue\uc2  at \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the recent strength in the Hong Kong dollar is mainly driven by rising market carry-trade activities and equity-related demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "As risks posed by the coronavirus on global economy are still evolving, financial markets will continue to see considerable volatility. The HKMA will continue to closely monitor the market situation and ensure Hong Kong's money and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets operate smoothly," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Joanne Chiu at joanne.chiu@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 21-04-20 1229GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020200421eg4l000gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
