\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  to Prop Up HKD Again -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 11:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2019, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1010 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday to prevent the local dollar from weakening past 7.85 to the dollar, the weakest level allowed under the financial hub's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system. The \uc2 HKMA\uc2  sold USD500 million and bought Hong Kong dollars in order to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly this month as flush liquidity in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial system has kept interest rates low, weighing on the local dollar, which traded at 7.8499 to the U.S. dollar in recent action. ( saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com ; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 0947 GMT - German Bund yields could go deeper into negative territory but the currently known economic backdrop makes it hard to justify a further fall, say \uc2 UBS\uc2  ' rates strategists. "Theoretically, there is no hurdle to prevent the German Bund yield from trading well below the all-time lows of -0.20% but the economic connotation such a scenario would carry is hard to justify based on what we currently know," the strategists say. The all-time low was reached in shortly after the Brexit vote. The 10-year Bund yield trades at -0.076%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0933 GMT - Foreign investors are dumping Turkish bonds to get hold of liras so that they can honor swap transactions, according to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . The yield on the two-year Turkish government bond has risen to 20.53% from 18.58% last Friday. The five-year credit default swaps, which enable investors to protect themselves from debt defaults, has jumped to 453 basis points from 312 bps a week ago, says SocGen. Lack of lira liquidity has dragged the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few days through the kind of tumultuous times it experienced back in August. Lira plunged Friday, then recovered at the beginning of this week, and it's falling again Thursday, with USD/TRY last up 3.5% at 5.5194. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0909 GMT - Perhaps in the assumption that the U.K. will avoid crashing out of the \uc2 EU\uc2  without a deal, investors are not protecting themselves against a severe fall in sterling following a worst-case Brexit scenario. The cost of two-week options in sterling against the U.S. dollar is nowhere near the levels it was before the Brexit referendum in 2016, and has actually fallen slightly in the past couple of days. The cost of options with other maturities is also relatively cheap. Moreover, risk reversals show a fall in the premium demanded to take out options to sell sterling against the euro in the next three months over those to buy it, which a \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analyst describes as "unjustifiable." (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0845 GMT - The yield on \uc2 Peugeot\uc2  's outstanding bonds drops after \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  said it upgraded its credit rating on the French car maker to Baa3, the lowest rung of the investment grade category, from junk. "Today's rating action reflects the continuous improvement in credit metrics since 2013," \uc2 Moody's\uc2  says. The yield on \uc2 Peugeot\uc2  's December 2024 bonds falls almost 5 basis points to 1.808% after the announcement, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . The rating upgrade comes months after S&P Global Ratings upgradedPeugeot to BBB-, the lowest level in the IG category, in mid-December. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0809 GMT - Borrowing costs in the eurozone will stay lower for longer, says S&P Global Ratings. Economists at the rating firm now expect the \uc2 ECB\uc2  's first rate increase to come in January 2020. "A more dovish \uc2 ECB\uc2  also means that the euro exchange rate will stay weak for another year, acting as a sort of buffer in a phase of weaker global trade," S&P says. The rating firm cuts its forecast for eurozone growth to 1.1% for 2019 but it expects a move back to trend and rebound to a 1.4% rate in 2020 and 2021, it says. On the back of lower energy prices, S&P expects inflation to slow to 1.3% this year from 1.8% in 2018. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0806 GMT - The 10-year German Bund yield continues to trade in negative territory with more room downward, even to as low as its all-time low of -0.20%, say \uc2 KBC Bank\uc2  's analysts. "The German 10-year [...] is on its way to revisit the all-time low," \uc2 KBC\uc2  says. The all-time low was reached in July 2016, in the aftermath of the Brexit vote. The 10-year Bund yield trades at -0.084%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0757 GMT - Sterling is holding up well despite U.K. legislators' failure to agree on a course of action for Brexit. Members of Parliament were on Wednesday given votes on a range of options, but no option managed to win the backing of a majority of the House. GBP/USD is down by 0.2% at 1.3161 and EUR/GBP rises 0.3% to 0.8550. "As a result the considerable risk of a no-deal outcome remains in place," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. "I lost any sort of lingering optimism over the past months - and whatever might have remained was lost last night," says an analyst at the German lender. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0738 GMT - Though the greenback has softened a bit after hitting a 2-week high earlier today versus the Singapore dollar, \uc2 UOB\uc2  says the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has scope to test S$1.3585 near-term before easing off. The investment bank concurs the greenback's strength the past day has exceeded its expectation as it broke S$1.3545. Meanwhile, it now pegs support at S$1.3520. The US dollar is off 0.05% at S$1.3546.(saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 0735 GMT - German 10-year Bund yields edge higher but still trade in negative territory, with the release of Germany's preliminary March inflation data being a potential key mover. "Today's weaker data should further fuel the repricing with tentative signs for depo cut expectations already emerging," say \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  's rates strategists. Germany's year-on-year price index measured according to EU-harmonized standards is expected to decline to 1.5% in March from 1.7% in February, according to economists' forecasts in The Wall Street Journal's survey. Further potential drivers of the day include an Italian government bond auction. The 10-year Bund yield trades at -0.082%, up about 0.6 basis points, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0627 GMT - Japanese stocks were the biggest decliners in Asia throughout today's trading, hit by fresh pressure from a rising yen and bond prices. The Nikkei slid 1.6% to 21033.76 while airlines was the only sector to not fall. Among the weakest industries was energy, pharmaceuticals and electronics--with some companies in each falling about 3.5%. Meanwhile, 10-year JGB yields have fallen 3 basis points to -0.10%, a fresh 2 1/2-year low, and the dollar has dropped to Y110.09 from Y110.44 late Wednesday in New York.(kosaku.narioka@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0511 GMT - Though this year's draft of Singapore's 10-to-15-year development master plan is positive for commercial landlords as it proposes enhanced plot sizes in the central business district, DBS says the aim to promote living closer to workplaces bodes well for residential's long-term outlook. "While we remain positive on longer-term trends in property prices, we believe a steady growth in supply of homes will likely be accompanied by more-conducive policies to ensure stable growth in the property market." Oversupply concerns continue to weigh on Singapore's residential-property market. DBS remains positive on Singapore REITs. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 28, 2019 06:10 ET (10:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020190328ef3s0011p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
