ng and the requirements of the Hong Kong Companies Ordinance Cap.622. \par  \par         These consolidated financial statements have been prepared under the historical cost convention, as modified by \par         the revaluation of investment properties, financial assets at fair value through other comprehensive income , \par         financial assets and financial liabilities held for trading, and financial assets and financial liabilities (including \par  \par         derivative instruments) at fair value through profit or loss, which are carried at fair value. \par  \par         The preparation of financial statements in conformity with HKFRSs requires the use of certain critical \par         accounting estimates. It also requires management to exercise its judgement in applying the Group's accounting \par         policies. \par  \par         Except as described below, the accounting policies and methods of computation used in the preparation of the \par         2018 consolidated financial statements are consistent with those used and described in the Group's annual \par         audited financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2017. \par  \par         The financial information in this results announcement is presented in thousands of Hong Kong dollars \par         (HK$'000), unless otherwise stated. \par  \par         (a)      New and amended standards adopted by the Group \par  \par         The following new and amended standards have been adopted by the Group for the first time for the financial \par         year beginning on or after 1 January 2018: \par  \par         (1)     HKFRS 9, "Financial instruments" \par  \par         The Group has adopted HKFRS 9 issued by the HKICPA with effect from 1 January 2018, which resulted in \par         changes in accounting policies and adjustments to the amounts previously recognised in the financial statements. \par  \par         As permitted by the transitional provisions of HKFRS 9, the Group elected not to restate comparative figures. \par         Any adjustments to the carrying amounts of financial assets and liabilities at the date of transition were \par         recognised in the opening retained earnings and other reserves of the current period. \par  \par         Consequently, for notes disclosures, the consequential amendments to HKFRS 7 disclosures have also only been \par         applied to the current period. The comparative period notes disclosures repeat those disclosures made in the \par         prior year. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                              4 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Banking Group Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2   \par  \par  \par 2.     Basis of Preparation and Accounting Policies (Continued) \par  \par        (a)      New and amended standards adopted by the Group (Continued) \par  \par        (1)     HKFRS 9, "Financial instruments" (Continued) \par  \par        The adoption of HKFRS 9 has resulted in changes in our accounting policies for recognition, classification and \par        measurement of financial assets and financial liabilities and impairment of financial assets. HKFRS 9 also \par        significantly amends other standards dealing with financial instruments such as HKFRS 7 "Financial \par        Instruments: Disclosures". \par  \par        Set out below are disclosures relating to the impact of the adoption of HKFRS 9 on the Group. \par  \par        The measurement category and the carrying amount of financial assets and liabilities in accordance with HKAS \par        39 on 31 December 2017 and HKFRS 9 at the opening of 1 January 2018 are compared and shown as follows: \par  \par        HK$'000                                    HKAS 39                                        HKFRS 9 \par                                             Measurement             Carrying               Measurement          Carrying \par        Financial assets                         category             amount        