alue of the Group's investment in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Chongqing\f28 \uc2 \f2   ("BOCQ") had been \par        below the carrying amount for approximately 60 months. On this basis, the Group continues to perform an \par        impairment test on the carrying amount of the investment in BOCQ to assess the recoverable amount. Based on \par        the assessment conducted in 2016 and before, the recoverable amount was assessed as higher than the carrying \par        amount, and no impairment needed to be recognised. \par  \par        The impairment test is performed by comparing the recoverable amount of BOCQ, determined by a value in use \par        ("VIU") calculation, with the carrying amount of the investment. The VIU calculation uses discounted cash flow \par        projections based on management's estimates of BOCQ's earnings and dividends to be paid in future, and the \par        estimated probable exit value in future after considering the growth of BOCQ and its net asset value for the \par        medium and longer term. The discount rate applied to the VIU calculation was estimated with reference to \par        BOCQ's cost of equity, which is publicly available in the market. \par  \par        In performing the VIU calculation to arrive at the recoverable amount of the investment, the Group considers all \par        relevant factors including market views and qualitative factors to ensure that the inputs to the VIU calculation \par        are appropriate. Adjustments need to be made to reflect the latest situation affecting BOCQ and also market \par        outlook for the medium and longer term that are relevant in projecting BOCQ's future performance. Significant \par        management judgement is required in estimating the future cash flows of BOCQ. \par  \par        Based on the assessment conducted for the position as at 31 December 2017, the recoverable amount, as \par        determined by the VIU calculation and after considering all relevant factors and valuation assumptions, was \par        lower than the carrying amount, and an impairment charge at HK$815 million had been recognised, which had \par        been included in the consolidated results of the Group for the year ended 31 December 2017. The written down \par        value of the investment as at 31 December 2017 (i.e. carrying amount less impairment allowance made of \par        HK$815 million as at the same date) was HK$4,134.7 million. \par  \par        In the impairment assessment carried out for the first half of 2018, the recoverable amount, based on the VIU \par        calculation, had dropped further below the carrying amount and an impairment charge of HK$403 million was \par        recognised in the Group's 2018 interim results. The latest impairment test performed for the position as at 31 \par        December 2018 concludes that the recoverable amount is assessed as lower than the carrying amount before \par        considering any impairment allowance made by HK$1,448 million. With impairment allowance totalling \par        HK$1,218 million already made up to 30 June 2018, an impairment charge of HK$230 million was recognised \par        in the consolidated results of the Group for the second half of 2018. As a result, the carrying amount of the \par        Group's investment in BOCQ at 31 December 2018 has been written down to HK$3,620.6 million, which is the \par        recoverable amount at 31 December 2018 assessed by the Group. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                          16 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Banking Group Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2   \par  \par  \par 11.    Taxation \par  \par        Hong Kong profits tax has been provided at the rate of 16.5% (2017: 16.5%) on the estimated assessable profit \par  \par        for the year. Taxation on overseas profits has been calculated on the estimated assessable profit for the year at \par        the rates of taxation prevailing in the countries in which 