her reserves (including retained earnings)                                21,186,848    20,813,523 \par  \par Shareholders' funds                                                 17      25,435,407    25,062,082 \par  \par Total equity                                                                31,992,448    31,436,403 \par  \par Total equity and liabilities                                               237,301,478   225,537,674 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                                 3 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Financial Holdings Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2   \par  \par  \par Note: \par  \par 1.      Statutory Financial Statements \par  \par         The information set out in this results announcement does not constitute statutory financial statements. \par  \par         Certain financial information in this results announcement is extracted from the Group's statutory \par         consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2018 (the "2018 financial statements") \par         which will be delivered to the Registrar of Companies and available from the website of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \par         Exchanges and Clearing Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2   in due course. The auditors have expressed an unqualified opinion on those \par         financial statements in their report dated 27 March 2019. \par  \par 2.      Basis of Preparation and Accounting Policies \par  \par         The consolidated financial statements of the Group have been prepared in accordance with all applicable \par         Hong Kong Financial Reporting Standards ("HKFRSs" is a collective term which includes all applicable \par         individual Hong Kong Financial Reporting Standards, Hong Kong Accounting Standards ("HKASs") and \par         Interpretations) issued by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Institute of Certified Public Accountants\f28 \uc2 \f2   ("HKICPA"), accounting \par         principles generally accepted in Hong Kong and the requirements of the Hong Kong Companies Ordinance \par         Cap.622. \par  \par         These consolidated financial statements have been prepared under the historical cost convention, as modified \par         by the revaluation of investment properties, financial assets at fair value through other comprehensive income, \par         financial assets and financial liabilities held for trading, and financial assets and financial liabilities (including \par         derivative instruments) at fair value through profit or loss, which are carried at fair value. \par  \par         The preparation of financial statements in conformity with HKFRSs requires the use of certain critical \par         accounting estimates. It also requires management to exercise its judgement in applying the Group's \par         accounting policies. \par  \par         Except as described below, the accounting policies and methods of computation used in the preparation of the \par         2018 consolidated financial statements are consistent with those used and described in the Group's annual \par         audited financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2017. \par  \par         The financial information in this results announcement is presented in thousands of Hong Kong dollars \par         (HK$'000), unless otherwise stated. \par  \par         (a)      New and amended standards adopted by the Group \par  \par         The following new and amended standards have been adopted by the Group for the first time for the financial \par         year beginning on or after 1 January 2018: \par  \par         (1)      HKFRS 9, "Financial instruments" \par  \par         The Group has adopted HKFRS 9 issued by the HKICPA with effect from 1 January 2018, which resulted in \par         changes in accounting policies and adjustments to the amounts previously recognised in the financial \par         statements. \par  \par         As permitted by the transitional provisions of HKFRS 9, the Group elected not to restate comparative figures. \par         Any adjustments to the carrying amounts of financial assets and liabilities at the date of transition were \par         recognised in the opening retained earnings and other reserves of the current period. \par  \par         Consequently, for notes disclosures, the consequential amendments to HKFRS 7 disclosures have also only \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2019 00:12 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Financial Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  . -3-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par         been applied to the current period. The comparative period notes disclosures repeat those disclosures made in \par         the prior year. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                              4 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Financial Holdings Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2   \par  \par  \par 2.     Basis of Preparation and Accounting Policies (Continued) \par  \par        (a)      New and amended standards adopted by the Group (Continued) \par  \par        (1)     HKFRS 9, "Financial instruments" (Continued) \par  \par        The adoption of HKFRS 9 has resulted in changes in our accounting policies for recognition, classification \par        and measurement of financial assets and financial liabilities and impairment of financial assets. HKFRS 9 also \par        significantly amends other standards dealing with financial instruments such as HKFRS 7 "Financial \par        Instruments: Disclosures". \par  \par        Set out below are disclosures relating to the impact of the adoption of HKFRS 9 on the Group. \par  \par        The measurement category and the carrying amount of financial assets and liabilities in accordance with \par        HKAS 39 on 31 December 2017 and HKFRS 9 at the opening of 1 January 2018 are compared and shown as \par        follows: \par  \par        HK$'000                                       HKAS 39                          