ailable in the market. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 27 Mar 2019 00:13 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Financial Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  . -8-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par        In performing the VIU calculation to arrive at the recoverable amount of the investment, the Group considers \par        all relevant factors including market views and qualitative factors to ensure that the inputs to the VIU \par        calculation are appropriate. Adjustments need to be made to reflect the latest situation affecting BOCQ and \par        also market outlook for the medium and longer term that are relevant in projecting BOCQ's future \par        performance. Significant management judgement is required in estimating the future cash flows of BOCQ. \par  \par        Based on the assessment conducted for the position as at 31 December 2017, the recoverable amount, as \par        determined by the VIU calculation and after considering all relevant factors and valuation assumptions, was \par        lower than the carrying amount, and an impairment charge at HK$815 million had been recognised, which \par        had been included in the consolidated results of the Group for the year ended 31 December 2017. The written \par        down value of the investment as at 31 December 2017 (i.e. carrying amount less impairment allowance made \par        of HK$815 million as at the same date) was HK$4,134.7 million. \par  \par        In the impairment assessment carried out for the first half of 2018, the recoverable amount, based on the VIU \par        calculation, had dropped further below the carrying amount and an impairment charge of HK$403 million \par        was recognised in the Group's 2018 interim results. The latest impairment test performed for the position as \par        at 31 December 2018 concludes that the recoverable amount is assessed as lower than the carrying amount \par        before considering any impairment allowance made by HK$1,448 million. With impairment allowance \par        totalling HK$1,218 million already made up to 30 June 2018, an impairment charge of HK$230 million was \par        recognised in the consolidated results of the Group for the second half of 2018. As a result, the carrying \par        amount of the Group's investment in BOCQ at 31 December 2018 has been written down to HK$3,620.6 \par        million, which is the recoverable amount at 31 December 2018 assessed by the Group. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                         16 \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dah Sing Financial Holdings Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2   \par  \par  \par 11.    Taxation \par  \par        Hong Kong profits tax has been provided at the rate of 16.5% (2017: 16.5%) on the estimated assessable \par        profit for the year. Taxation on overseas profits has been calculated on the estimated assessable profit for the \par        year at the rates of taxation prevailing in the countries in which the Group operates. \par  \par        Deferred taxation is calculated in full on temporary differences under the liability method at the tax rates that \par        are expected to apply in the year when the liability is settled or the asset is realised. \par  \par  \par         HK$'000                                                                                               2017 \par                                                                                            2018 \par  \par         Current income tax: \par         - Hong Kong profits tax                                                                            381,825 \par                                                                                        389,775 \par         - Overseas taxation                                                                                 45,705 \par                                                                                         41,7