\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Hong Kong dollar weakens in sync with rising Chinese stock market\b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 01:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story sent late on Thursday with no changes)               \par \par \uc2 * HKD hits weak end of band, c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  5 times in 2 weeks               \par \par \uc2 * Yuan rallies, heavy A-share purchases via Hong Kong year-to-date               \par \par \uc2 * Excessive cash in banking system sustaining \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness               \par \par \uc2 By Noah Sin               \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, March 21 (Reuters) - Heavy demand for China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from investors keen to bet on the mainland's surging stock markets is pressuring the Hong Kong dollar and depleting cash balances in the city.               \par \par \uc2 The jump in demand for yuan  has pushed the Hong Kong dollar to the weak end of its narrow trading band since early March. Cash balances in Hong Kong's banking system are still high but have been gradually falling.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep it within its 7.75-7.85 band against the U.S. dollar.               \par \par \uc2 It has bought HK$11.6 billion ($1.48 billion) in five \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year. All took place this month, including three this week.               \par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still trading at 7.8475 per U.S. dollar, close to the weak end of the band.               \par \par \uc2 The protracted weakness is partly driven by rising appetite for Chinese A-shares in recent months, said Ronald Man, a \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  in Hong Kong.               \par \par \uc2 That is because offshore investors, including Hong Kong-based funds and individuals, largely buy into domestic Chinese markets via the Hong Kong-hosted Stock Connect, which requires them to exchange other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the yuan.               \par \par \uc2 China's A-share market has jumped around 24 percent this year, driven by hopes that a long-running Sino-U.S. trade war will end soon and buoyed by Beijing's policies to support economic growth. Global index provider MSCI's decision to quadruple China's weighting in its benchmark index has also led to heavy foreign investment inflows.               \par \par \uc2 Flows into China, known as northbound flows, under the Connect scheme hit 121 billion yuan ($18.09 billion) in January and February, 3.73 times more than the same period last year.               \par \par \uc2 Demand for yuan in Hong Kong has risen as investors chased the rally, said Bruce Yam, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at local broker Everbright Sun Hung Kai.               \par \par \uc2 "We've had some big orders from clients, retail mostly, since Chinese New Year," he said.               \par \par \uc2 The yuan is up 2.8 percent this year, and the yuan deposit pool in Hong Kong, the largest offshore yuan centre, declined by 2.6 percent to 599.1 billion in January, according to HKMA. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hkma.gov.hk/eng/key-information/press-releases/2019/20190228-6.shtml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.hkma.gov.hk/eng/key-information/press-releases/2019/20190228-6.shtml}}}\uc2  ].               \par \par \uc2 Simon Derrick, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon in London, says the negative correlation between the Chinese and Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early December is at odds with past trends, noting that historically a weaker yuan had put pressure on Hong Kong's equity markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .                              \par \par \uc2 AGGREGATE IMPACT               \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar could recover as the ample cash in its banking system, a hangover of the synchronised easing by global central banks, is reduced and as yields rise.               \par \par \uc2 With investors borrowing Hong Kong's low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fund their A-share purchases, capital has been leaving the city's banks. Yet, Hong Kong's markets have been flush with cash and yields have therefore not yet reacted to the outflows.               \par \par \uc2 The aggregate balance, which reflects liquidity levels in the banking system, stands at HK$68.9 billion, despite HK$7.4 billion being absorbed by the HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "Until you bring it down to at least HK$10 billion, at global financial crisis levels, it's unlikely that HK rates would rise in a significant way," said Man.               \par \par \uc2 Norman Chan\uc2 , chief executive of the HKMA, said in a statement on Thursday that the wide spread between U.S. and Hong Kong interest rates will continue to lure funds away from the city.               \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's one-month interbank borrowing rate lagged its U.S. counterpart by 1.58 percentage points in late February, the highest in over a decade.               \par \par \uc2 The spread has narrowed to about 90 basis points this week. Pressure for it to widen again is easing after the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  shelved projected 2019 rate hikes on Wednesday. ($1 = 6.6900 Chinese yuan renminbi) ($1 = 7.8477 Hong Kong dollars)               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-3-22T01:00:10.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190322ef3m0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
