\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  as  \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong \highlight\uc2  dollar weakens, buys HK$1.5 bln\b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 05:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds HKMA statement)\par \par \uc2 March 9 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again on Saturday in London and U.S. trading hours, buying HK$1.51 billion in Hong Kong dollars as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly hit the lower end of its allowable trading band.\par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will reduce the aggregate balance - the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA - to HK$74.8 billion on March 12, according to Reuters data. HKMA announced the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mid-Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Howard Lee\uc2 , the authority's deputy chief executive, said the main reason for the move was the significant widening of the interest rate gaps between the Hong Kong dollar and U.S. dollar after the year-end, mainly because of the drop in banks\u8217\'20\'19 funding demand, which led to a fall in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interbank interest rates. The Hong Kong dollar was weakened as traders sold the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for U.S. dollars, he said.\par \par \uc2 The local dollar breached the weaker end of its trading range at 7.85 per U.S. dollar for the first time in almost six months on March 6, and has hit that level repeatedly since.\par \par \uc2 Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 Lee said the HKMA would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the large gap between HKD and USD remained, which would likely keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak in the near future.\par \par \uc2 HKMA last stepped into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Aug. 28, when it sold $1 billion worth of U.S. dollars for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 7.85, as the Hong Kong dollar reached its band's weak side.\par \par \uc2 Excess cash in Hong Kong's banking system has kept interest rates low and caused the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken since the start of 2019, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 In February, the one-month inter-bank rate (HIBOR) was lagging its dollar equivalent the most since January 2008, leading investors to borrow cheaply in the Hong Kong dollar to buy higher-yielding U.S. dollar assets and spurring capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 That gap has since narrowed but stays at 2008 levels. (Reporting by Twinnie Siu, Noah Sin and Kane Wu; writing by Noah Sin; Editing by Stephen Coates) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-3-9T05:54:35.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190309ef3900691\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
