\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan Also Rebounds on Trade-Talk Plans -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2018\par 08:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0602 GMT - Asian equities rebounded this morning on signs that the US and China plan to resume trade talks. It also boosted the yuan, and its early bounce has continued to build. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now up 1% onshore at CNY6.88/dollar after nearing CNY7 in the offshore market yesterday. That level has stoked fears of capital outflows in the past. \uc2 China's Commerce Ministry\uc2  said today that a vice minister will travel to the US at Treasury's invitation; no date was specified. Still, it's been enough to boost the beaten-down \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But analysts note talks would involve lower-level officials than those in May. The escalation in trade tensions between the US and China has hit the yuan hard, driving it down 6.7% offshore the past 2 months. (saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 0433 GMT - Today's fresh record low for the dollar versus the rupee, following yesterday's holiday and late Tuesday's India trade data, comes as analysts say \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness will offset the recent pullback in oil prices, keeping the current-account deficit at elevated levels. \uc2 Sujan Hajra\uc2 , chief economist at Anand Rathi Securities, thinks the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain market stability but that the \uc2 RBI\uc2  doesn't have a particular target for the rupee. The dollar is up 0.4% at INR70.17. (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0350 GMT - Though perking up some in the wake of yesterday's surprise-to-some rate hike, \uc2 Nomura\uc2  says further declines for the Indonesian rupiah "cannot be ruled out". With foreign ownership of local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds still high and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  having relatively limited \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, \uc2 Nomura\uc2  says the rupiah remains vulnerable. The investment bank has added further to its dollar-long position against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and predicts another quarter-point hike at next month's \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting. The rupiah is down 7.6% this year versus the dollar. (joanne.chiu@wsj.com; @joannechiuhk)\par \par \uc2 0331 GMT - \uc2 Nomura\uc2  says the recent drop in the Thai government's popularity ratings to the lowest level since 2014's military takeover at 51% raises the risks of a yet-another election delay and populist policies. "The fiscal-spending mix will likely shift towards short-term policies at the expense of long-term productive public-investment spending." The election is currently due for February; it's the 6th promised data, according to the Bangkok Post. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0255 GMT - Fresh lows could wait the Indian rupee today as 1-month non-deliverable forwards are pointing to the dollar opening at around INR70.20 in the spot market, versus Tuesday's record of INR70.08 and after yesterday's local holiday. Today's pressure could come from late Tuesday's trade data, with July's deficit the largest in 5 years amid increase oil imports. That pressure the country's current-account deficit, making the rupee more vulnerable. (manju.dalal@wsj.com: @manjudalalsg)\par \par \uc2 0251 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, in 3 separate overnight actions selling a combined $1.9 billion to keep the greenback's trading band with the Hong Kong dollar intact. It's the 3rd-biggest day since the moves began in April and the most since April 18's $2.3 billion of greenback sales. The latest move will reduce the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  to HK$92.61 billion ($11.8 billion) tomorrow. It's the 1st time since 2008 the measure of interbank liquidity will have breached HK$100 billion. (joanne.chiu@wsj.com; @joannechiuhk)\par \par \uc2 0248 GMT - Markets in Asia are almost totally different from 90 minutes ago. Then, wide 1%-plus declines were seen in a number of stock indexes in the wake of fresh overnight selling in the US and Tencent's 2Q report. But with chatter of a meeting between American and Chinese officials on trade in the coming days, sentiment has quickly got sunny. And not just in equities but also Treasury yields and oil prices rising, gold paring its decline and the yen moving off session lows. The Nikkei finished morning trading up 0.1% after falling as much as 1.5% earlier. Hong Kong's benchmarks are slightly higher as well, with Tencent now off just 2%. S&P 500 futures are up 0.4%. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 0232 GMT - Australia's drop in July employment was the first since February, coming after June's growth was revised higher to 58,200. The 3-month growth after through last month was a still-healthy 22,500, and in January the past year's increase was a record 427,100. It was always going to be difficult to maintain such strength. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0222 GMT - Australia's surprise July employment decline isn't a sign the country's economy has suddenly hit the brakes, says \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  ' \uc2 Paul Dales\uc2  , reminding that the data series' normal volatility means there is occasionally declines even as underlying trends are healthy. Even so, he says the labor market won't be strong enough to trigger a decent rise in wage growth for a while yet. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0205 GMT - Hitting the yen in the past half-hour or so is news that China's vice commerce minister has been invited to visit the US for trade talks. Michiyoshi Kato at \uc2 Mizuho Bank\uc2  says expectations are growing for possible improvement in the countries' fight even as officials from both appear to maintain a strong posture toward each other. Many in the markets are hoping "they'll shake hands behind closed doors" to prevent further worsening of the situation, he adds. The dollar is above Y110.80, versus an earlier low of Y110.46. Asian equities have also rebounded strongly, with the Nikkei off just 0.1% after an earlier decline of 1.5%. (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0156 GMT - Though Australia's unemployment rate hit levels last seen in November 2012 last month at 5.3%, that's because fewer people were looking for work. Meanwhile, a drop in part-time employment more than offset gains for full-timers, resulting in a surprise overall decline. Still, it all should be good news for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looking for lower unemployment, stronger wage growth and higher inflation. The Aussie dollar jumped to session highs on the news, and is widely up some 0.2% versus other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0129 GMT - [Dow Jones ] Expect the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  to aggressively tighten policy in October after its two rate increases in June and August, says ING. State elections in the remainder of this year and general elections in 2019 should lead investors to add a political-risk premium to local assets, further hurting the Indian rupee, it says. "A multi-year high trade deficit, elevated inflation, and signs of slowing GDP growth -- haven't been any friendlier," ING says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dropped 8.6% this year versus the dollar, the steepest among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it says. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 16, 2018 02:02 ET (06:02 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180816ee8g000dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
