\par\par \b \uc2 Italian Government Bond Yields Edge Higher -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2018\par 13:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1114 GMT - Italian government bonds underperform their peers in the eurozone, with the 10-year BTP yield rising versus slight declines elsewhere. The 10-year BTP yield is trading 1.1 basis point higher at 3.06%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . "Some investors remain concerned that there are voices in the [Italian] governing coalition, especially in the League, that are not committed to the EU ," says \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  . Bond yields move inversely to prices. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 1112 GMT - U.S. retail sales due at 1230 GMT could serve as further proof that "U.S. consumer continues to support GDP growth and would likely keep the Fed anchored to a four-rate hike cycle this year," says BK Asset Management. This could send USD/JPY to 112 as the week proceeds, BK AM says. USD/JPY is last flat Wednesday at 111.11. A WSJ poll projects that overall sales have risen only 0.1% month-on-month in July, however, compared with a 0.5% rise in June. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1049 GMT - Atlantia's bond yields surge further on Tuesday, after the Italian government has reportedly withdrawn the concession of the Italian autostrade network from the Italian company, according to local newspaper La Repubblica. \uc2 Atlantia\uc2  is also said to be receiving a fine of EUR150 million, after a bridge on a highway that \uc2 Atlantia\uc2  manages in the port city of Genoa, Italy, collapsed on Tuesday. The death toll has risen to around 37, according to media reports. Yields on Atlantia's July 2027 EUR bonds, which have a coupon of 1.875%, rise to 2.718%, a record high, according to Tradeweb.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 1046 GMT - The South African rand has followed the fall in the Turkish lira in the past few days as the Turkish crisis had made investors worry about other emerging market countries. The Institute of International Finance says South Africa is one of the countries which has seen strong inflows of foreign money when non-resident portfolio flows to EM rebounded sharply after the China devaluation scare in 2015/6. This leaves South Africa "vulnerable" to greater outflows, the IIF says. Indonesia, Lebanon, Egypt and Colombia are also "especially at risk." (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1045 GMT - At times of falling bond prices it's easy to forget that the return of a bond portfolio is made up of both price movements and accrued coupon payments over time, says Jeremy Smouha, chief executive officer of Atlanticomnium, the asset manager of credit opportunities strategy at \uc2 GAM\uc2 . "Especially in a year like this one, when year-to-date performance across most credits has been negative, in aggregate," Mr. Smouha says. Coupons accrue slowly on a day-to-day basis and price movements can disguise the attractiveness of an individual bond's return, he adds. Yields rise when bond prices fall. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 1032 GMT - Hong Kong's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought more Hong Kong dollars in Asian trading hours to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg with the greenback. The latest purchase of US$300 million worth of Hong Kong dollars by the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes after it bought $275 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars during US trading hours Tuesday, the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May. That move will reduce the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  to HK$104.89 billion ($13.36 billion) on August 17. During April and May, \uc2 HKMA\uc2  bought a combined HK$70.35 billion to defend the city's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (joanne.chiu@wsj.com ; @joannechiuhk)\par \par \uc2 1031 GMT - Turkish banks have a "high level of probability to work out a non-performing loan problem" due to a "very high level of profitability" says \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  . This is because Turkish banks make pre-provisioning profits of 4.5% of total loans each year, it says. \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  says that the issue for Turkish banks is that Turkey's non-performing loans (NPLs) ratio, currently at 4.5%, could end up rising to levels seen in a normal emerging market recession or crisis of around 20%. This would equate to about 40% of Turkish banks' CET1. Turkish banks' high profitability levels combined with lower leverage ratios of around 10 times would make Turkish banks resilient to a recession-like NPLs ratio, says \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  . (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 1007 GMT - More and more people have become concerned that the U.K. will exit from the \uc2 European Union\uc2  without a deal on March 31 next year, says BNY Mellon. This is "a point reflected in the current political betting with odds of 4/6 being offered on this outcome." But the U.K. could also ask for an extension to the Article 50 to have another general election and choose a government which would be able to agree on what kind of a relationship it wants with the EU . Or it could hold another Brexit referendum. None of these scenarios that BNY Mellon sees possible include a soft Brexit option. The pound has been falling due to these uncertainties. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0958 GMT - The 2.5% rise in U.K. inflation in July "represents a peak," ING analysts say, adding they expect inflation "to begin trending downwards over the next few months gradually." Oil prices, which were behind the rise, are expected to fall. Moreover, "the impact of the pound's post-Brexit plunge is continuing to fade." This means that the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  will "remain on the sidelines for the next few months, as Brexit uncertainty becomes an increasing concern." (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0942 GMT - Despite concerns about further weakening in the Chinese yuan, \uc2 Schroders\uc2 ' Shanghai CIO Jack Lee doesn't expect a drastic depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the prospect of major capital outflows isn't something Beijing wants to see. "It's probably not right to be overly bearish" on the yuan, he contends while highlighting the recent move by Beijing to reimpose a requirement that makes it more expensive to bet against the yuan. Meanwhile, he says the recent weakness in Chinese tech stocks mean the sector is "entering into a more-maturing stage" after a half-dozen years of growth driven by constant innovation and rising penetration rates. (joanne.chiu@wsj.com; @joannechiuhk)\par \par \uc2 0935 GMT - This year's rate hikes from \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  may not be done, says \uc2 OCBC\uc2 , as the Fed is poised to continue its cycle of increases. That as "the prospect of further trade tensions between the US and China or the US with other countries could further" dampen sentiment towards the rupiah, which hit 3-year lows versus the dollar this week. That as the investment bank is predicting 5.1% GDP growth for Indonesia this year, the lower end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0911 GMT - Unlike previous easing cycles in which China's policy makers stimulated both infrastructure and property investment, this time around Beijing will likely shun the latter--at least initially--says \uc2 Nomura\uc2 . The investment bank contends that apart from a changing mentality toward financial risks, a lack of consensus on the best strategies among the top leadership may also result in a different policy path this go-around. It thinks Beijing will probably keep putting deleveraging on hold until it "feels the imminent risk of financial and growth instability is cleared." Property investment has been holding up this year despite a sharp slowdown in overall investment, official data show. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 15, 2018 07:14 ET (11:14 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180815ee8f00184\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
