\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong Dollar May Get Some Support Soon -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 930 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2018\par 04:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0244 GMT - After requiring more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar could get support starting in mid-June from a raft of potential liquidity-squeezing events that could start to drive up short-term interbank rates, says \uc2 OCBC\uc2 . They include another fed hike, several large IPOs in the pipeline and large dividend payouts. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been at or near the week end of its trading band with the greenback, for more than a month. To date, the city's de-factor \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought more than HK$70 billion (US$8.9 billion) to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including HK$5.99 billion in 2 moves during New York trading on Friday. (chester.yung@wsj.com; @chester_yung)\par \par \uc2 0241 GMT - \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  is the latest investment bank to no longer \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  standing pat the rest of the year. It predicts a quarter-point hike in August, though adds it could come next month, as inflation is picking up amid higher oil prices and a beaten-down rupee. It could all make foreign investors skittish. The bank thinks a 2nd 2018 hike could be needed if oil remains at or above $80/barrel; it briefly breached that level last week. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0237 GMT - Australia's securities commission and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have created central new methodology for the bank-bill swap rate, a major benchmark for the Australian dollar and widely referenced in many financial contracts. BBSW will now be calculated directly from market transactions during a longer rate-set window and involve a larger number of participants than before. The move is seen anchoring the rate to real transactions at traded prices. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0215 GMT - Any more trade deals between China and the US could accelerate the decline of China's current-account surplus and added to long-run depreciation pressure for the yuan, says \uc2 UBS\uc2  . Beijing has agreed to cut its trade surplus with the US by boosting imports, but rejected a US request for a $200 billion reduction in the bilateral trade gap. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0147 GMT - The joint statement from the US and China on trade means talks will continue and new tariffs aren't imminent but ruling out a possible trade war can't be done yet, say Macquarie economists. They note the statement failed to mention key issues like the China 2025 plan or \uc2 ZTE\uc2 , adding that trade imbalances could still be a "strategic weapon" used by the US against China. (liyan.qi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0130 GMT - China guided the yuan to its weakest level since Jan. 24 against the dollar amid the greenback's persistent gains. The \uc2 PBoC\uc2  put today's trading midpoint for the dollar at CNY6.3852, versus CNY6.3763 on Friday. It ended onshore trading then at CNY6.3760. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0118 GMT - Retail volumes in New Zealand were much softer than implied by monthly retail-card spending in 1Q, and notably short of expected. Spending-data trajectory has weakened, and \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  adds fading population growth and visitor arrivals are adding to headwinds. Meanwhile, monthly net immigration flow slowed 8% in April from March. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0103 GMT - There were 2,089 homes taken to auction across Australia's capital cities last week, with a preliminary successful-sales rate of 60%. That after 2,279 auctions were held a week earlier and the final clearance rate dropped to 58%, the lowest since December 2015, says \uc2 CoreLogic\uc2  . In Melbourne, Australia's largest auction market, the preliminary clearance rate was 64%, versus 60% a week earlier. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0011 GMT - New Zealand seasonally-adjusted net migration monthly inflows slipped 460 to 4,930 in April from March, with two thirds of the decline driven by fewer arrivals and one third by higher departures. The annual net inflow is now sitting just over 67,000, down from nearly 68,000 in March and a peak of 72,400 in July last year. ANZ says the April figures reaffirm its view that the net migration cycle is gradually easing. (james.glynn@wsj.com ; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 2354 GMT - It was a soft start to the year for New Zealand retail spending, rising just 0.1% from 4Q last quarter. \uc2 Westpac\uc2  says that signals downside risk to 1Q GDP and chimes with other signs the country's economy is slowing. The bank expects household-spending growth to be modest the coming year amid a cooling housing market in response to government-policy changes. Population growth is also expected to ease gradually. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 2313 GMT [Dow Jones ] Population growth absorbed most of the 400,000 jobs that Australia created last year, helping to keep wages low. But it's also having a more puzzling effect. "Immigration should be boosting aggregate consuming spending," says \uc2 Carl Weinberg\uc2 , chief economist at \uc2 High-Frequency Economics\uc2 . "A 3.2% increment to the population means more mouths to feed, more people to clothe and house, and more consumption of all goods and services." Yet real retail sales growth was close to zero last year and hasn't budged much since, Weinberg says. That's frustrating the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  , which can't seem to shift inflation from the bottom of its target band. (david.winning@wsj.com; @dwinningWSJ)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 20, 2018 22:45 ET (02:45 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180521ee5l00040\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
