\par\par \b \uc2 BREAKINGVIEWS-Higher rates are likely to calm Hong Kong property\b0\par\par\uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2018\par 03:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (The author is a Reuters Breakingviews columnist. The opinions expressed are his own.)\par \par \uc2 By Christopher Beddor\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, May 8 (Reuters Breakingviews) - Higher rates are likely to calm Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s frothy property market. Interbank lending is getting more expensive after a decade-long slump, pointing to costlier mortgages and slower price growth. This will be manageable for banks and developers, and welcome for renters and retailers.\par \par \uc2 House prices have been on a tear \u8211\'20\'13 as have those of offices, shops and warehouses. Second-hand home prices surged more than 30 percent in two years, according to Midland Realty, a broker. Nowadays $1 million, or HK$7.8 million, will not stretch to much more than a one-bedroom apartment on Hong Kong island. Officials have toyed with various countermeasures, such as hiking stamp duty for some buyers, but to little avail.\par \par \uc2 Change may now be coming from an unexpected quarter. \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  started selling U.S. dollars in mid-April to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in turn draining liquidity. That has helped to nudge up the benchmark 3-month interbank lending rate to around 1.7 percent. For the previous ten years it had averaged slightly under 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 These changes will feed into housing, since many mortgages are linked to the interbank rate. Analysts at Mizuho reckon a 1 percentage point increase in mortgage rates could trigger a 10.5 percent decline in home prices, assuming the basic ratio of prices to incomes remains constant.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, rates are only one factor, alongside other concerns like demand from mainland China and the pace of government land sales. Even so, sustained higher rates will cool price growth for houses and commercial property.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s likely to prove manageable for Hong Kong banks such as \uc2 HSBC\uc2  , \uc2 Bank of East Asia\uc2  and the local arm of Bank of China, which lend extensively against property but typically at conservative loan-to-value ratios. Most of the city\u8217\'20\'19s large banks could handle a 30 percent decline in property prices without it denting their creditworthiness, reckons S&P Global Ratings. Property developers would see profit growth tail off, but start from a position of robust financial health.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, this would be excellent news for the territory\u8217\'20\'19s would-be homebuyers and renters, including, on the commercial side, many retailers. After years of double-digit price increases, they are unlikely to mind a bit of a cool-down.\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cbeddor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/cbeddor}}}\par \par \uc2 CONTEXT NEWS\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Norman Chan\uc2 , the chief executive of the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , warned that the public should prepare for possible volatility in local interest rates and asset markets after the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee concluded its latest meeting on May 2 without a change to interest rates.\par \par \uc2 - Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must follow American rates in order to maintain its peg to the U.S. dollar, under which the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is maintained at a rate of between 7.75 and 7.85 to the dollar. It started \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets on April 12 to prop up the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the most recent system was introduced in 2005, although it has previously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in periods of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.\par \par \uc2 - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases, which have the effect of draining liquidity in the territory, have helped lift the benchmark 3-month interbank lending rate to more than 1.7 percent.\par \par \uc2 - For previous columns by the author, Reuters customers can click on\par \par \uc2 - SIGN UP FOR BREAKINGVIEWS EMAIL ALERTS: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://bit.ly/BVsubscribe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://bit.ly/BVsubscribe}}}\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Quentin Webb and Katrina Hamlin) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-8T02:34:27.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180508ee58001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
