\par\par \b \uc2 Problems Near, Far Ram Hong Kong Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joanne Chiu \par \uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2018\par 11:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 It was a good day for Hong Kong's stock exchange -- it landed the massive \uc2 Xiaomi Corp\uc2 . initial public offering-listing, but the rest of the city's stocks couldn't manage to win.\par \par \uc2 Myriad factors -- local and abroad -- combined to conspire against Hong Kong equities Thursday as the city's stocks continue struggling for traction following February's low for many markets globally.\par \par \uc2 Be it U.S.-China trade tensions, interest-rate worries or the weakened \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar needing government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there has been plenty to keep investors up at night lately.\par \par \uc2 The Hang Seng Index fell 1.3% Thursday, among the bigger drops in Asia, partially on worries about the potential impact of continued U.S. interest-rate increases. That's despite the news on Xiaomi's IPO -- a long-sought prize for the stock exchange, which followed a change in listing rules that came into effect Monday.\par \par \uc2 The ongoing rate-increasecycle could pull some investment funds out of Asia, said Eugene Leow, a rates strategist at DBS. As such, there might be a need for more prudent monetary policies across the region, he said.\par \par \uc2 Norman Chan\uc2 , the head of Hong Kong's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on Thursday warned of possible volatility in local interest rates and asset markets. Local liquidity is seen tightening gradually as capital continues to flow out of the city, he said, "providing a more conducive environment" for Hong Kong interest rates to increase.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday night said that mainland investors wouldn't be able to use a preapproved quota program to buy assets abroad denominated in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That stoked concerns "about the flow of funds from China into Hong Kong" as rumors circulated about Beijing putting fresh curbs on outward investments by insurers and asset managers, said Castor Pang, head of research at Core Pacific-Yamaichi International.\par \par \uc2 Daniel So, a strategist at \uc2 China Merchants Bank\uc2 , expects the city's stock market to remain weak thanks to fund-flow concerns, which have helped push the Hong Kong dollar back to the weak end of its trading band against its U.S. counterpart.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month bought a total of 51.3 billion Hong Kong dollars, funding that with the sale of US$6.5 billion, in more than a dozen transactions to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nearly 35-year-old link to the greenback. In the same month, Chinese investors pulled out of Hong Kong stocks at the fastest pace since markets in Shanghai and the city were linked in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Mr. So predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to come under added pressure near-term from Friday's debut of Ping An Healthcare, Hong Kong's biggest initial public offering so far this year. That deal generated more than HK$350 billion of orders from local retail investors, and orders require money to be put up ahead of a potential purchase.\par \par \uc2 The retail portion of the deal received 654 times more orders than the stock initially set aside for that investor class; the amount for local investors has been quadrupled. Ping An Healthcare is selling HK$8.8 billion of stock.\par \par \uc2 Issues away from Hong Kong also weighed on stocks Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Aside from the Hong Kong dollar's weakness, potential fresh U.S. action against Chinese telecom-equipment makers \uc2 ZTE Corp\uc2 . and \uc2 Huawei Technologies Co\uc2 . sparked concerns about fund outflows, said Hayman Chiu, research director at \uc2 Cinda International\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Headlines the past few weeks involving the two telecom-equipment makers have hit some Hong Kong-listed tech names, notably smartphone-parts makers \uc2 Sunny Optical Technology Group Co\uc2 . and \uc2 AAC Technologies Holdings Inc\uc2 . \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 03, 2018 05:53 ET (09:53 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180503ee5300171\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
