\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA\uc2  May Change Reserves Makeup Post- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 2018\par 05:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0308 GMT - As \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent HK$3.26 billion ($415 million) within the past day to prop up the local dollar, \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  thinks the \uc2 HKMA\uc2  may reallocate its portfolio. As of the end of 2016, only 7.8% wasn't in the US or \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars. Meanwhile, the investment bank believes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could total some HK$80 billion the next month or two. That compares with more than HK$640 billion during the financial crisis and HK$147 billion after 2015's Chinese yuan devaluation. (chester.yung@wsj.com; @chester_yung)\par \par \uc2 0304 GMT - The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightening monetary policy possibly shows that market jitters about trade tension "have not impacted the real economy's activity yet," says \uc2 Song Seng Wun\uc2  , an economist at CIMB Private Bank. While the US and China have been "talking tough, the follow-through...remains minimal" so far. The MAS had a neutral stance on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy for 2 years, and whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves again in October will depend on economic growth, he posits. The economist predicts GDP will rise 3.2% this year after 2017's 3.6%. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0258 GMT - With Chinese visitors logging their first annual monthly increase in a year, South Korea's retail sales logged a 2nd-month of gains in March. Chinese tourists usually splash out on cosmetics and other local goods at Korean stores, and the government's green-book report shows sales at leading department stores and discount chains respectively rose 6% and 15% from a year earlier in March. That as Chinese tourists climbed 13%; visitors from there slumped last year amid Korea's deployment of a US missile-defense system that Beijing opposes. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com; @kwanwoo)\par \par \uc2 0247 GMT - The \uc2 World Bank\uc2  has raised Malaysia's 2018 gross domestic product growth view to 5.4% from its 5.2% forecast in January, flagging continued strength in private consumption, according to \uc2 World Bank\uc2  's East Asia and Pacific Economic Update report. The new projection is still lower than the 5.5%-6.0% projected by \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its latest annual report issued last month and last year's growth of 5.9%. The \uc2 World Bank\uc2  says public capital spending will likely decline after strong growth last year, but will be partially offset by a continued expansion of exports and private investment. Further ahead, it sees Malaysia's economy expanding 5.1% in 2019 and 4.8% in 2020. (yantoultra.ngui@wsj.com; @yantoultra)\par \par \uc2 0225 GMT - The market is showing little inclination of a Hong Kong dollar's trading band not holding as it has hit the weak end at points during the past 24 hours. One-year forward contracts are around HK$7.7950-60, almost exactly the band's midpoint. In 2015, when a break of the convertibility band was being priced in for the first time since the Asian financial crisis, similar contracts were trading above HK$7.90. The weak end of the trading band is at HK$7.85. \uc2 RBC\uc2 's Sue Trinh adds implied volatility on a 1-year forward basis is also low. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0220 GMT - \uc2 BofA Merrill Lynch\uc2  expects the Hong Kong dollar to remain at its weakest level against the greenback for the rest of the year. The USD/HKD pair will stay at 7.85 while 3-month Hibor rate will rise to 1.6% by year-end, the bank estimates, from 1.17% as of Thursday. Still, a full convergence of the local dollar rate with US Libor is unlikely, \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  says since it believes Hong Kong dollar rates "only need to rise to the extent where investors find it insufficiently attractive to invest in overseas assets." That will require around HK$80 billion of HKD purchases by the city's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  estimates. The \uc2 HKMA\uc2  bought a combined HK$3.2 billion as of Friday morning. (joanne.chiu@wsj.com; @joannechiuhk)\par \par \uc2 0211 GMT - Global markets might be underpricing the risk of another financial-system shock, \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warns while contending that current asset pricing suggests investors see little chance of adverse outcomes. As such, a news surprise could lead to a disruptive and lasting correction across markets. Potentials triggers could include sharp interest-rate rises in the absence of stronger economic growth as well as a jump in global inflation or inflationary expectations, the \uc2 RBA\uc2  says. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0155 GMT - Consensus was split on whether Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would tighten today, and \uc2 RBC\uc2 's Sue Trinh was among those expecting no. But with the dollar nominal effective exchange rate mostly near the middle of its trading band, "a modest change in slope would not be very impactful in the near-term anyway." She adds the MAS may also find itself quickly reversing today's modest tightening stance if the China-US trade war "turns nasty." The Singapore dollar is at pre-release levels versus the greenback after seeing a knee-jerk gain as 1Q GDP came in stronger than expected. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0151 GMT - As Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  flags future inflation risks in tightening today, others in Asia don't appear to be in a hurry to do the same. While South Korea and Malaysia have done quarter-point interest-rate hikes within the past 6 months, there's been no rush to follow up and other central banks remain on the sidelines. Many economists think Philippines may become the next Asian one to tighten, with weakness in the peso seen as a major factor in doing so. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0149 GMT - Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may tighten policy further in October, says Continuum Economics, as it seems to be watchful of rising inflation risks. "We had been flagging that the buoyant economic outlook should filter through to domestic-oriented sectors and also increase price pressures." The MAS tightened for the first time in 6 years today as steady economic growth is expected to be repeated this year. GDP rose an estimated 4.3% in 1Q after 4Q's 3.6%, it was separately reported Friday. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh)\par \par \uc2 0125 GMT - China guides the yuan slightly weaker against the dollar despite gains in onshore trading yesterday as the greenback rose overnight. Today's trading midpoint was set at CNY6.2898, versus CNY6.2834 yesterday. The dollar ended onshore trading at CNY6.2814. (kenan.machado@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0108 GMT - \uc2 Moody's\uc2  upgrade for Indonesia could trigger more inflows into Indonesian assets. "This could potentially reduce the fundraising costs for the government," says \uc2 Mandiri Sekuritas\uc2  debt-market analyst Handy Yunianto. But he also noted that US yields and the rupiah's outlook could cause some to pause before adding to holdings in Indonesian's rupiah bonds. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 12, 2018 23:08 ET (03:08 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180413ee4d0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\